---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/landing/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/landing/Footer.astro';

const title = "PRIVACY";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="fixed inset-0 noise-bg pointer-events-none z-50"></div>
  <div class="fixed top-[-10%] right-[-5%] w-[600px] h-[600px] gradient-sphere pointer-events-none -z-10"></div>
  
  <Navbar />
  <main class="relative pt-32 max-w-[1600px] mx-auto px-8 min-h-screen">

<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="mb-24">
    <h1 class="font-headline font-bold text-7xl md:text-9xl leading-[0.9] tracking-tighter neon-glow mb-8">
        PRIVACY
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-on-surface-variant max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Simple, honest, and straightforward.
    </p>
</section>

<!-- Sections -->
<section class="space-y-8 mb-32 max-w-4xl">

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/10">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The App</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed mb-4">
            TajsOS is a local-first application. The data you create (nodes, protocols, journals) is stored on your device in a local database.
            We do not have a central cloud that ingests your personal data by default.
        </p>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            If you choose to use the experimental synchronization server, the server will hold a copy of the synced data. The sync server is intended to be self-hosted.
            There is currently no telemetry, analytics, or hidden tracking built into the core open-source app.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/10">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The Website</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            This website is a static site built to document the project. It may be hosted on platforms (like GitHub Pages, Vercel, or Netlify) that collect standard web server access logs (IP address, user agent, timestamps).
            We do not use invasive third-party tracking scripts or advertising cookies on this documentation site.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl border border-outline-variant/10">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            As an experimental project, these practices may evolve. If telemetry or hosted services are introduced in the future, they will be strictly opt-in and clearly documented.
        </p>
    </div>

</section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
